<title>DUBAI: Iran pardons 962 prisoners to mark Shi'ite feast.</title>
<headline>Iran pardons 962 prisoners to mark Shi'ite feast.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iran will free or reduce the jail terms of 962 prisoners under a pardon approved by supreme leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei, Tehran radio said on Friday.</p>
<p>The pardon, marking the Shi'ite Moslem feast of Eid al-Ghadir on Saturday, covered prisoners convicted by military and revolutionary courts, the radio said.</p>
